$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(4'-tert-Butyl-2',6'-dimethylphenylsulfinyl)-3-fluoropyrrolidine (22,
1:1 mixture) Step 1: Into a stirred solution of 175 mg (2.0 mmol) of ( ±
)-3-pyrrolidinol in 3 mL of dry dichloromethane, was added 0.4 mL of 7:3
wt% HF-pyridine (Sigma-Aldrich), followed by slow addition of a solution
of 626 mg (2.5 mmol) of 1k in 2 mL of dry dichloromethane. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 4 hours at room temperature. Step 2: Into the
reaction mixture above, 6 mL of triethylamine was added very slowly. Heat
and fume were generated during addition. After addition, the reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 2 hours. Dichloromethane (25
mL) was added to the reaction mixture. The reaction mixture was washed
with water three times, dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate, and
filtered. Removal of solvent gave crude product, which was then purified
by preparative TLC using ether:haxane (2:1) as an eluent to give 505 mg
(85%) of 22 (1:1 mixture of diastereomers) (NMR chart No. 22a):
N-(4'-tert-Butyl-2',6'-dimethylphenylsulfinyl)-3-fluoropyrrolidine (22,
1:1 mixture), yield 100%. M.p. 110-111 °C; 19F NMR (CDCl3) δ -173.33 (m,
0.5F), -174.50 (m, 0.5F); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.98 (s, 2H), 5.22 (dm, J =
53.6 Hz, 1H), 3.05-3.80 (m, 4H), 2.53 (s, 6H), 1.90-2.30 (m, 2H), 1.27
(s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 153.4, 137.5, 137.4, 135.0, 134.7, 127.5, 93.5
(d, J = 177.7 Hz, isomer 1), 93.1 (d, J = 178.4 Hz, isomer 2), 53.6 (d, J
= 23.8 Hz, isomer 2), 51.5 (d, J = 23.8 Hz, isomer 1), 46.5 (isomer 1),
43.9 (isomer 2), 34.5, 33.6 (d, J = 21.7 Hz, isomer 1), 33.2 (d, J = 21.7
Hz, isomer 2), 31.2, 20.0; IR (neat) 2965, 1593, 1456, 1363, 1227, 1129,
1092, 985, 870, 695 cm-1. HRMS (ESI/APCI method) Calcd for C16H24FNNaOS
(M + Na)+: 320.1455. Found: 320.1461. Anal Calcd for C16H24FNOS: C,
64.61%; H, 8.13%; N, 4.71%. Found: C, 63.98%; H, 7.98%; N, 4.66%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions with Et3N(HF)3 gave lower yield,
exothermic in stage 2, alternative reaction conditions in one step gave
lower yield but some stereoselectivity, fluoropolymer vessel preferred
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
