$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-7-1-3. Fluorination of (2S, 4R)-N-Fmoc-4-hydroxyprolinonitrile (11) A
solution of 0.97 g (3.9 mmol) of 1k in 2 mL of dry dichloromethane was
added slowly to a stirred solution of 0.64 g (2.6 mmol) of (2S,
4R)-N-Fmoc-4-hydroxyprolinonitrile (11) in 3 mL of dry dichloromethane in
a fluoropolymer vessel cooled in an ice bath. After complete addition,
the mixture was stirred for 1 h under cooling on an ice bath and then at
room temperature for 60 h. 19F NMR analysis using a standard (C9H19F)
showed that the yield of product was quantitative. All the volatiles were
removed at reduced pressure and the residue was dissolved in a mixture of
2 mL of dichloromethane and 2 ml of ether. Into the solution, anhydrous
pentane was added in excess, and the resulting solid was collected and
chromatographed on silica gel using a 1:1 mixture of ethyl acetate and
hexane as an eluent to give (2S,4S)-N-Fmoc-4-fluoroprolinonitrile (12) as
a colorless solid. Yield: 1.43 g (85%).
(2S,4S)-N-Fmoc-4-fluoroprolinonitrile (12), yield 1.43 g (85%). M.p.
106-107 °C; 19F-NMR (CDCl3) δ -174.63 (m); 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.25-7.85 (m,
8H), 5.30 (d, J = 51.2 Hz, 1H), 4.20-4.85 (m, 4H), 3.45-4.0 (m, 2H),
2.15-2.75 (m, 2H); 13C-NMR (CDCl3) δ (as a mixture of two rotamers) a
major rotamer: 153.9, 143.6 (m), 141.5, 128.0, 125.2, 120.2, 117.8, 91.8
(d, J = 178.0 Hz), 68.2, 52.8 (d, J = 24.6 Hz), 47.2, 45.8, 37.0 (d, J =
21.7 Hz); a minor rotamer: 153.5, 143.6 (m), 141.4, 127.3, 125.0, 120.2,
118.0, 90.8 (d, J = 179.2 Hz), 68.6, 53.3 (d, J = 24.6 Hz), 47.2, 45.3,
38.0 (d, J = 21.7 Hz); HRMS (EST/APCI method) Calcd for C20H17FNaO2
(M+Na)+: 359.1166. Found: 359.1164.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (toxic byproduct HF), fluoropolymer vessel used, various reagents
and conditions used to remove byproducts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
