$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
fluoroalkane standards13,14 To a 0.33 M solution of the corresponding
alcohol (1.0 equiv.) in dry dichloromethane at 0 °C, was added
dimethylaminosulfur trifluoride (1.05 equiv.)in one portion using a
plastic needleless syringe. The resulting solution was stirred for 30 min
at 0 °C, allowed to warm to ambient temperature, and poured over ~25 g of
crushed ice. Once the ice melted, the organic phase was separated and the
aqueous phase was extracted with dichloromethane (3 X 10mL). The combined
organics were washed with brine (10 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and filtered.
The solvent was then removed by rotary evaporation. Kugelrohr
distillation afforded the corresponding fluoride. 1-fluoroundecane (2):
1-Undecanol15 (176 mg, 1.02 mmol) was subjected to the general
fluoroalkane standard synthesis procedure. Kugelrohr distillation (10
mmHg) afforded fluoride 2. (3-fluorobutyl)benzene (7):
4-Phenylbutan-2-ol19 (91 mg, 0.61 mmol) was subjected to the general
fluoroalkane standard synthesis procedure. Kugelrohr distillation (30
mmHg) afforded fluoride 7. 7, clear colorless oil, quantitative yield 19F
{1H} NMR (282 MHz): δ -139.7, -174.5 ppm.
