$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Evaluation of deoxyfluorination in different solvents In an N2-filled
glovebox, an oven-dried vial was charged with N,N’-1,3-bis(2,6-
diisopropylphenyl)imidazolium chloride (68.9 mg, 0.150 mmol, 1.50 equiv),
previously dried (200°C, 24 hours) CsF (152 mg, 1.00 mmol, 10.0 equiv)
and a phenol (0.100 mmol, 1.00 equiv). Solvent (1.0 mL) was added and the
vial was sealed, then removed from the glovebox. The mixture was stirred
at 23°C for 30 min and subsequently heated at 100 °C, 110°C or 140°C for
24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to 23°C, then
1-fluoro-3-nitrobenzene (10.0 μL, 0.0939 mmol, 0.939 equiv) was added to
the mixture. The yields were determined by comparing the integration of
the 19F NMR (470 MHz, 23°C) resonance of 4-fluoro-1,1’-biphenyl (-117.2
ppm), 1-fluoro-4-methoxybenzene (-126.8 ppm) or 1-fluoro-2-methoxybenzene
(-137.1 ppm) with that of 1-fluoro-3-nitrobenzene (-112.0 ppm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, alternative reaction conditions shown, 19F-NMR yield, yield
depends on reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM PhenoFluorMix: Practical Chemoselective Deoxyfluorination of Phenols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fujimoto, Teppei; Ritter, Tobias
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(3), 544-547

