$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Gram scale synthesis of (8α, 9R)-6’-fluorocinchonan-9-ol acetate An
oven-dried flask was charged with PhenoFluorMix (6.23 g). PhenoFluorMix
was heated at 140°C for 1 hour under vacuum (~0.1 Torr). After the
mixture was cooled to 23°C, O-acetyl (8α, 9R)-cinchonan-6’,9-diol
9-acetate4 (1.00 g, 2.83 mmol) was quickly added. The flask was evacuated
and backfilled with N2 gas, then toluene (28 mL) was added via syringe.
The mixture was stirred at 23°C for 30 min and subsequently heated at
110°C for 24 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to 23°C, then
filtered through a pad of Celite eluting with CH2Cl2 (3 × 15 mL). The
filtrate was concentrated in vacuo and the residue was purified by flash
silica gel column chromatography (MeOH in EtOAc = 0%-10%). 998 mg of the
title compound as a light yellow oil (98% yield). R f = 0.24 (MeOH in
EtOAc = 5%). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 23°C, δ): 8.84 (d,
J = 4.4 Hz, 1H), 8.11 (dd, J = 9.3, 5.4 Hz, 1H), 7.86 (dd, J = 10.3, 2.5
Hz, 1H), 7.48 (td, J = 8.3, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 7.41 (d, J = 4.9 Hz, 1H), 6.33
(d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 5.85 (m, 1H), 5.04-4.98 (m, 2H), 3.35 (q, J = 8.3,
1H), 3.07 (m, 1H), 3.00 (dd, J = 13.7, 9.8, 1H), 2.62 (m, 1H), 2.54 (m,
1H), 2.26 (br s, 1H), 2.10 (s, 3H), 1.96 (m, 1H), 1.85 (m, 1H), 1.71 (m,
1H), 1.55 (m, 1H), 1.45 (dd, J = 13.7, 7.3 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3, 23°C, δ): 170.2, 160.7 (d, J = 248.0 Hz), 149.4 (d, J = 1.9 Hz),
146.0, 145.0 (d, J = 5.7 Hz), 141.8, 133.1 (d, J = 9.5 Hz), 127.0 (d, J =
9.5 Hz), 119.9, 119.6 (d, J = 25.8 Hz), 114.7, 107.4 (d, J = 22.9 Hz),
74.3, 59.6, 56.7, 42.3, 39.8, 27.9, 27.6, 25.2, 21.1. 19F NMR (470 MHz,
CDCl3, 23°C, δ): -114.6. HRMS-FIA(m/z) calc’d for C21H24FN2O2 [M+H]+,
355.1816; found, 355.1832.
