$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (17) General procedure for deoxofluorination. To a stirred suspension of
diethylaminodifluorosulfinium tetrafluoroborate (4.0 mmol) in
dichloromethane (25 mL) at room temperature was added the substrate (2.67
mmol) and triethylamine trihydrofluoride (4.0 mmol). The resulting
mixture was stirred under nitrogen over the prescribed amount of time.
The reaction was then quenched at room temperature with a 5% sodium
bicarbonate aqueous solution and stirred for 15 minutes, and the
resulting mixture was extracted twice using dichloromethane. The organic
phases were combined, dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and
concentrated. The residual oil was purified by SiO2 chromatography.
1-Fluoro-3-phenylpropane. The titled compound was prepared according to
the foregoing procedure using 3-phenylpropanol (reaction time = 4h).
Column chromatography (pentane) of the residual material yielded
1-fluoro-3-phenylpropane (314mg, 85%) as a clear liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3)
7.4-7.1 (m, 5H), 4.47 (dt, J = 47.3, 5.9 Hz, 2H), 2.76 (t, 7.3 Hz, 2H),
2.1-1.9 (m, 2H); 19F NMR (CDCl3) -220.56 (m, 1F); 13C NMR (CDCl3) 141.21,
128.59, 128.57, 126.13, 83.25 (d, 164.5 Hz), 32.15 (d, 19.6 Hz), 31.42
(d, 5.7 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Aminodifluorosulfinium Tetrafluoroborate Salts as Stable and Crystalline
Deoxofluorinating Reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beaulieu, Francis; Beauregard, Louis-Philippe; Courchesne, Gabriel;
Couturier, Michel; LaFlamme, Francois; L'Heureux, Alexandre
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
