$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure: The alcohol (1 equiv) was
dissolved in EtOAc (concentration of 0.5 M) at ambient temperature. The
solution was cooled to 5 °C and Et3N·3HF (2 equiv) and Et3N (2 equiv)
were successfully added in a dropwise manner. After stirring for 5 min,
TFFH was added in one portion (1.5 equiv). The solution was then allowed
to stir at the necessary temperature. Upon completion, the reaction was
quenched with sat. NaHCO3 to pH 7 and diluted with additional EtOAc.
Layers were separated and the organic layer was concentrated to a crude
residue. The crude residue could be purified by flash chromatography or
partitioned between MTBE and H2O to remove the tetramethylurea byproduct.
Entry 3, Temperature: 23°C, Time: 1 h, Ratio of RF/elim: 10:1, Yield:
90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tetramethylfluoroformamidinium hexafluorophosphate (TFFH) as a mild
deoxofluorination reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bellavance, Gabriel; Dube, Pascal; Nguyen, Bao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2012), 23(4), 569-572

