$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):RGT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 1006064-01-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-5. Fluorination of benzyl alcohol with
different arylsulfur trifluorides In a 10 mL fluoropolymer (PFA) bottle
equipped with a nitrogen inlet tube, septum, and a magnetic stir bar, 65
mg (0.604 mmol) of benzyl alcohol was added to a stirred solution of
0.664 mmol of arylsulfur trifluoride in 3 mL of anhydrous
dichloromethane. The addition was performed at room temperature under a
stream of nitrogen. The mixture was allowed to stir at room temperature.
After 2 h, a yield of benzyl fluoride was determined by 19F NMR analysis
of the reaction mixture. The results are shown in Table 1. Benzyl
fluoride, yield 95%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM fluoropolymer bottle used, optimized on arylsulfur trifluoride reagent,
optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
