$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(Allyloxy)-4-(bromomethyl)benzene (6). To a solution of 5 (100 mg,
0.609 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (4 mL), CBr4 (404 mg, 1.2 mmol) was added
followed by portion wise addition of triphenyl phosphine (191 mg, 0.73
mmol) at 0 °C under argon atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred at
0 °C for 30 min and then at ambient temperature for 12 h. It was quenched
with saturated sodium bicarbonate solution (15 mL) and the aqueous phase
was washed with CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed
with brine (20 mL), dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was evaporated under
vacuum. Since the final compound was unstable, the residue was purified
by flash column chromatography and the crude product was directly used
for the next step. Chromatography was performed with ethyl
acetate:cyclohexane (2:8) to yield an off-white colored gummy mass.
1-(Allyloxy)-4-(bromomethyl)benzene (6). , yield (133 mg, 96 %)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fluorinated Isatin Derivatives. Part 2. New N-Substituted
5-Pyrrolidinylsulfonyl Isatins as Potential Tools for Molecular Imaging
of Caspases in Apoptosis
