$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Deoxofluoro-arylsufinylation of ethylene
glycol A solution of 0.991 g (3.96 mmol) of 1k in 1 mL of dry
dichloromethane was slowly added to a stirred solution of 0.246 g (3.96
mmol) of ethylene glycol and 0.800 g (7.72 mmol) of triethylamine in 3 mL
of dry dichloromethane in a fluoropolymer vessel cooled on an ice bath.
The reaction mixture was stirred on an ice bath for 1 h and then at room
temperature for 15 h. An aq. saturated sodium bicarbonate solution was
added to the reaction mixture, which was then extracted with
dichloromethane. The organic layer was separated, washed with water,
dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate, and filtered. Removal of solvent
at reduced pressure gave a residue, which was then thin-layered
chromatographed on silica gel using ether:hexane (1:5) as an eluent to
give 2-fluoroethyl 4-tert-butyl-2,6-dimethylbenzenesulfinate (18) as a
colorless solid. Yield: 0.927 g (86%). trans-2-Fluorocyclopentyl
4-tert-butyl-2,6-dimethylbenzenesulfinate (19) (95:5 mixture), oil, yield
95%. 19F NMR (CDCl3) minor, δ -178.9 (m, 0.07F*); major, -179.8 (m,
0.93F*) (*this isomer ratio is that of the isolated product); 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 7.04 (s, 2H), 4.98 (dm, J = 40.9 Hz, 1H), 4.78 (m, 1H), 2.62
(s, 6H), 1.75-2.25 (m, 6H), 1.29 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 154.9, 138.5,
137.2, 127.1, 98.0 (d, J = 179.2 Hz), 83.6 (d, J = 28.2 Hz), 34.6, 31.0,
30.2 (d, J = 20.9 Hz), 21.0, 19.3; IR (neat) 2966, 1593, 1456, 1406,
1227, 1195, 1132, 1081, 1032, 951, 871, 757, 615 cm-1. Anal Calcd for
C17H25FO2S: C, 65.35%; H, 8.07%. Found: C, 64.99%; H, 8.19%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (toxic byproduct HF), 95:5 dr, fluoropolymer vessel used,
alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
