$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Boc-cis-4-fluoro-L-proline methyl ester (4) Under N2 atmosphere, an
oven-dried 20 mL vial was charged with N-Boc-trans-4-hydroxy-L-proline
methyl ester (100 mg, 0.408 mmol, 1.00 equiv), KF (47.4 mg, 0.816 mmol,
2.00 equiv), and PhenoFluor (261 mg, 0.612 mmol, 1.50 equiv). Toluene
(6.5 mL) was added, followed by N,N-diisopropylethylamine (105 mg, 142
μL, 0.816 mmol, 2.00 equiv). The reaction mixture was stirred in a sealed
vial and heated at 80 °C for 16 h. Once cooled to 23 °C, the reaction
mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel, eluting with hexanes/EtOAc 4:1 (v/v), to
afford 93.0 mg of the title compound. N-Boc-cis-4-fluoro-L-proline methyl
ester (4), colorless solid (92% yield) Rf = 0.35 (hexanes/EtOAc 4:1
(v/v)). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): [mixture of
2 rotamers] 5.18 (d, J = 52.7 Hz, 1H, major + minor), 4.51 (d, J = 9.7,
1H, minor), 4.40 (d, J = 9.7 Hz, 1H, major), 3.72 (s, 3H, major + minor),
3.54–3.88 (m, 2H, major + minor), 2.53–2.23 (m, 2H, major + minor), 1.46
(s, 9H, minor), 1.41 (s, 9H, major). 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6, 100 °C, δ)
5.25 (d, J = 53.2 Hz, 1H) 4.37 (dd, J = 10.0, 1.7 Hz, 1H) 3.49–3.69 (m,
2H) 3.65 (s, 3H) 2.44–2.60 (m, 1H) 2.16–2.29 (m, 1H) 1.39 (s, 9H). 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 172.5, 172.1, 154.2, 153.9, 92.4 (d, JCF
= 178.5 Hz), 91.4 (d, JCF = 177.6 Hz), 80.6, 80.6, 57.8, 57.5, 53.4 (d,
JCF = 23.8 Hz), 53.1 (d, JCF = 23.8 Hz), 52.6, 52.4, 37.7 (d, JCF = 22.0
Hz), 36.8 Hz (d, JCF = 22.0 Hz), 28.6, 28.5. 19F NMR (375 MHz, CDCl3, 23
°C, δ): -173.7 and 173.3. Mass Spectrometry: HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z): Calcd
for [C11H18FNO4 + Na]+, 270.1112. Found, 270.1112.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Late-Stage Deoxyfluorination of Alcohols with PhenoFluor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sladojevich, Filippo; Arlow, Sophie I.; Tang, Pingping; Ritter, Tobias
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(7), 2470-2473

