$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Fluoroepoxide 11 N-(Trimethylsilyl)morpholine (414 µL, 2.33 mmol) was
added dropwise to a solution of Deoxo-Fluor® (429 µL, 2.33 mmol) in
anhydrous dichloromethane (8.4 mL) at -78 °C. The solution was stirred
for 2.5 hours at room temperature. The solution was then cooled to -78 °C
and a solution of 10 (138 mg, 0.389 mmol) in anhydrous dichloromethane
(26 mL) was added via cannula. The mixture was then heated to reflux for
19 hours and then concentrated onto silica. Purification was performed
using flash chromatography (1:0→17:3 dichloromethane/ethyl acetate). 11
as a yellow solid (130 mg, 94%). m.p. 158-162 °C; [α]D -9 (c 0.077,
CHCl3); IR (neat) ν max (cm-1) 3747, 3652, 3467, 3275, 1712, 1519, 1392,
1345, 1004; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.15 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H,
p-nitrophenyl), 7.83-7.70 (m, 4H, phthalimide ArH), 7.50 (d, J = 8.5 Hz,
2H, p-nitrophenyl), 5.40 (dd, J = 46.9, 5.09 Hz, 1H, CHF), 4.05 (dd, J =
14.3, 4.4 Hz, 1H, CHH), 3.75 (dd, J = 14.3, 5.6 Hz, 1H, CHH), 3.34-3.28
(m, 2H, O(CH)2); 13C {1H} NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.7, 148.2, 142.5, (d,
J = 21.6 Hz, C-CHF), 134.4, 131.6, 126.8 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, CH-C-CHF),
126.7, 123.8, 123.5, 91.0 (d, J = 180.5 Hz, CHF), 58.2, (d, J = 26.7 Hz,
CH-CHF), 52.3 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, CH-CH-CHF), 38.3; 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3)
δ -187.9 (dd, J = 47.0, 13.5 Hz, 1F, CHF); 19F {1H} NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3)
δ -187.9 (s, 1F, CHF); MS (APCI, +ve) m/z 357 (MH+, 27%), HRMS (ESI, +ve)
C18H13FN2O5Na+ requires m/z 379.0701, found 379.0708.
