$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-1,2:5,6-di-O-isopropylidene-α-D-allofuranose (5) Under
N2 atmosphere, an oven-dried 20 mL vial was charged with
1,2:5,6-di-O-isopropylidene-α-D-allofuranose (100 mg, 0.384 mmol, 1.00
equiv), KF (44.6 mg, 0.768 mmol, 2.00 equiv), and PhenoFluor (246 mg,
0.576 mmol, 1.50 equiv). Toluene (7.0 mL) was added, followed by
N,N-diisopropylethylamine (99.3 mg, 134 μL, 0.768 mmol, 2.00 equiv). The
reaction mixture was stirred in a sealed vial and heated at 80 °C for 16
h. Once cooled to 23 °C, the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo.
The residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel, eluting with
hexanes/EtOAc 8:1 (v/v), to afford 83.5 mg of the title compound.
3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-1,2:5,6-di-O-isopropylidene-α-D-allofuranose (5),
colorless oil (83% yield) Rf = 0.28 (hexanes/EtOAc 8:1 (v/v)). NMR
Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 5.97 (d, J = 3.9 Hz,
1H), 5.02 (d, J = 51.3 Hz, 1H), 4.72 (dd, J = 10.7, 3.4 Hz, 1H),
4.36–4.26 (m, 1H), 4.20–4.08 (m, 2H), 4.05 (dd, J = 8.5, 4.6 Hz, 1H),
1.52 (s, 3H), 1.47 (s, 3H), 1.38 (s, 3H), 1.34 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 112.5, 109.7, 105.3, 94.0 (d, JCF = 182.2 Hz), 82.7 (d,
JCF = 32.0 Hz), 80.8 (d, JCF = 19.2 Hz), 72.1 (d, JCF = 7.30 Hz), 67.3,
27.0, 26.9, 26.4, 25.3. 19F NMR (375 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): –209.9. Mass
Spectrometry: HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z): Calcd for [C12H19FO5 + Na]+,
285.1109. Found, 285.1099.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Late-Stage Deoxyfluorination of Alcohols with PhenoFluor
