$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure. KF (10 mmol) was added to a mixture of 5 mmol alcohol,
and 12.5 mmol triphenyl phosphine dissolved in 5 cm3 CCl4-DMF (1:4). The
mixture was stirred at room temperature. After completion of the reaction
(TLC), the mixture was extracted with 2 x 5 cm3 of n-pentane. The
combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4) and the solvent was removed
under reduced pressure to isolate the crude product, which was further
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (ethyl acetate:n-hexane =
1:9). 4-HO-C6H4-CH2F, yield 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
