$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-7-1-2. Fluorination of
2-methyl-1-phenyl-2-propanol A solution of 3.00 g (20 mmol) of
2-methyl-1-phenyl-2-propanol in 10 ml of dry dichloromethane was slowly
added into a stirred solution of 5.02 g (20 mmol) of 1k in 20 mL of dry
dichloromethane cooled on an ice bath. After stirred for 0.5 h, the ice
bath was removed and the stirring was continued at room temperature for 3
h. The solvent was removed from the reaction mixture at reduced pressure
and the resulting residue was mixed with 100 mL of 1N NaOH solution.
After it was stirred well for 5 min, the mixture was extracted with
dichloromethane (50 mLx2). The organic layer was washed with water, dried
over anhydrous magnesium sulfate, and filtered. After removal of solvent,
the residue was chromatographed on silica gel using hexane as an eluent
to give 2-fluoro-2-methyl-1-phenylpropane (24) as a colorless oil. Yield:
2.74 g, 90%. Table S1, Run 15, yield 91%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (toxic byproduct HF), product includes 14% racemic product and 2%
structural isomer, fluoropolymer vessel preferred
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
