$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure The alcohol 4, TBAT in the
amount indicated, base, and solvent (8 mL/mmol) were added in turn at the
temperature indicated. Then PBSF (2.2 equiv) was introduced and stirring
was continued for the time given. The final reaction mixture was directly
assayed by HPLC or LC-MS, and the calculation of HPLC data gave
conversion, dr value, and ratio of fluorination product/elimination
product in the mixture. The final reaction mixture was then concentrated
under reduced pressure and purified by flash chromatography (eluent: PE
to PE-acetone) to give (2S,4S)-3a, and a mixture of 5 and 6 (not
separated). Benzyl 2-fluoro-2-phenylacetate (3j), colorless oil, yield
91%. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.21 (dd, J= 42.5, 10 Hz, 2 H), 5.82 (d,
J= 39.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.17~7.51 (m, 10 H); IR (NaCl) ~ν 3036, 2961, 1760,
1683, 1266, 1057, 735, 696 cm-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A highly efficient conversion of primary or secondary alcohols into
fluorides with n-perfluorobutanesulfonyl fluoride-tetrabutylammonium
triphenyldifluorosilicate
