$DATUM 1-(Allyloxy)-4-(chloromethyl)benzene (26). To a solution of 5 (2.0 g,
12.1 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (15 mL), thionyl chloride (2.9 mL, 24.3 mmol)
was added dropwise (in 10 min) and the reaction mixture was stirred for
1-1.5 h at ambient temperature. The reaction mixture was evaporated
completely under vacuum and the residue was purified by column
chromatography (ethyl acetate:cyclohexane 3:7) to yield an oil. Yield:
2.05 g (90 %). 1-(Allyloxy)-4-(chloromethyl)benzene (26). , yield: 2.05 g
(90 %). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 4.53 (dt, 1H, 3JHa+Hb,Hc = 5.3
Hz, 3JHa+Hb,Hd+He = 1.5 Hz, ArOCHaHbCHc=CHdHe), 4.55 (s, 2H, Ar-CH2Cl),
5.30 (ddd, 1H, 2JHd,He = 2.8 Hz, 3JHd,Hc = 10.5 Hz, 4JHd,H = 1.4 Hz,
ArOCHaHbCHc=CHdHe), 5.37-5.44 (ddd, 1H, 2JHe,Hd = 3.2 Hz, 3JHe,Hc = 17.3
Hz, 4JHe,H = 1.6 Hz, ArOCHaHbCHc=CHdHe), 6.10 (ddt, 1H, 3JHc,H = 5.3 Hz,
3JHc,Hd = 10.5 Hz, 3JHc,He =17.3 Hz, ArOCHaHbCHc=CHdHe), 6.88 (d, 2H,
3JH,H =8.7 Hz, ArH), 7.29 (d, 2H, 3JH,H =8.7 Hz, ArH). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ (ppm) 46.3 (ArCH2Cl), 68.9 (ArOCH2CH=CH2), 114.9 (2C, ArCH),
117.8 (ArOCH2CH=CH2), 129.9 [ArC(CH2Cl)], 130.1 (2C, ArCH), 133.0
(ArOCH2CH=CH2), 158.7 [ArC(O-allyl)]. MS (GC-MS-EI): m/e (intensity %)
182 (38) [M+], 147 (100) [M+-Cl], 107 (37) [M+-C3H4Cl], 91 (23) [C7H7 +],
77 (67) [C6H5 +].
