$DATUM 6-epi-6-Fluoro-6-deoxy-galantamine (11) Under N2 atmosphere, an
oven-dried 20 mL vial was charged with free-based galantamine (100 mg,
0.348 mmol, 1.00 equiv), KF (40.4 mg, 0.696 mmol, 2.00 equiv), and
PhenoFluor (221 mg, 0.522 mmol, 1.50 equiv). Toluene (5.5 mL) was added,
followed by N,N-diisopropylethylamine (121 μL, 0.696 mmol, 2.00 equiv).
The reaction mixture was stirred in a sealed vial and heated at 80 °C for
12 h. Once cooled to 23 °C, the reaction mixture was concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel, eluting
with Et2O/MeOH 20:1 (v/v), to afford 89.0 mg of the title compound as a
10:1 mixture of two epimers at C-6 (89% yield). An analytically pure
sample of the major isomer was obtained after recrystallization from
EtOAc. 6-epi-6-Fluoro-6-deoxy-galantamine (11), (89% yield), colorless
solid Rf = 0.20 (Et2O/MeOH 10:1 (v/v)). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 6.64 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H) 6.58 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H)
6.14 (dd, J = 10.7, 1.5 Hz, 1H) 5.92 (t, J = 11.7 Hz, 1H) 5.42 (dt, J =
49.8, 7.3 Hz, 1H) 4.60 (br. s., 1H) 4.06 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H) 3.84 (s,
3H) 3.64 (d, J = 15.1 Hz, 1H) 3.25 (t, J = 13.7 Hz, 1H) 3.07 (d, J = 14.6
Hz, 1H) 2.88–2.97 (m, 1H) 2.38 (s, 3H) 2.19 (td, J = 14.2, 2.0 Hz, 1H)
1.88–1.99 (m, 1H) 1.68 (dd, J = 13.7, 2.0 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 146.5, 143.8, 132.4, 129.3, 128.3, 127.4, 121.6, 111.0,
87.7 (d, JCF = 12.8 Hz), 85.1 (d, JCF = 162.0 Hz), 60.4, 55.9, 54.1,
48.3, 42.2, 34.0 (d, JCF = 1.8 Hz) 29.4 (d, JCF = 19.2 Hz). 19F NMR (375
MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): -181.0. Mass Spectrometry: HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z):
Calcd for [C17H20FNO2 + H]+, 290.1551. Found, 290.1548.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used, sealed vial used
