$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure. KF (10 mmol) was added to a
mixture of 5 mmol alcohol, and 12.5 mmol triphenyl phosphine dissolved in
5 cm3 CCl4-DMF (1:4). The mixture was stirred at room temperature. After
completion of the reaction (TLC), the mixture was extracted with 2 x 5
cm3 of n-pentane. The combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4) and the
solvent was removed under reduced pressure to isolate the crude product,
which was further purified by column chromatography on silica gel (ethyl
acetate:n-hexane = 1:9). Cyclohexyl fluoride, yield 89%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Practical and General Method for Direct Synthesis of Alkyl Fluorides from
Alcohols under Mild Conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
