$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,1’-Dibromo-3,4,5,6-tetrafluoro-o-xylene PBr3 ( 4.94ml, 52mmol, 3eq )
was slowly added to a stirred solution of 1,2-bis(hydroxylmethyl)
3,4,5,6-tetrafluorobenzene (3.64g, 17.3mmol, 1eq) in 100ml of anhydrous
diethyl ether at 0°C. The reaction mixture was refluxed for 3 hours with
the condenser connected to a drying tube, cooled to R.T., poured to
ice/water. The organic layer was separated, washed with brine and dried
with anhydrous MgSO4 .Organic solvent was removed under reduced pressure.
1,1’-Dibromo-3,4,5,6-tetrafluoro-o-xylene was yielded as light yellow oil
(5,13g, 88%). 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ(ppm): 4.61 (t, J=1.2Hz, 4H). This 1H-NMR
spectrum is in accordance with the reported one1.
