$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of
4-(4-bromophenyl)-6-(1-fluoroethyl)-2-methylpyrimidine (±)-4a from (±)-5.
To a solution of (±)-5 (0.34 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (7 mL) at -10°C under argon
was added, dropwise, DAST (0.76 mmol, 2.2 eq). After 1h at -10°C the
mixture was neutralized with NaHCO3. The organic layer was separated,
washed, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under vacuum to afford an
orange oil. After purification on a silica gel column (Pentane/AcOEt 9/1)
pyrimidine (±)-4a was obtained as a pale yellow solid (86.0 mg, 86%
yield) Synthesis of
(-)-4-(4-bromophenyl)-6-(1-fluoroethyl)-2-methylpyrimidine (-)-4a from
(-)-5. The same conditions as described previously were used. Pyrimidine
(-)-4a was obtained as a pale yellow solid (86.8 mg, 87% yield). Chiral
HPLC Data (Column CHIRALCEL ADR 150*4.6, eluent Methanol/Water 90/10,
1.2mL/min, detection at 225 nm): retention times for (-)-4a: 6.9 min, for
(+)-4a: 8.9 min, a 96.4% ee was derived for the above (-)-4a sample. Mp
35°C. [α]20;D = -1.1 (c = 0.56, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Flexible Synthesis of Pyrimidines with Chiral Monofluorinated and
Difluoromethyl Side Chains
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bannwarth, Pierre; Valleix, Alain; Gree, Danielle; Gree, Rene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(12), 4646-4649

