$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-androsterone (13) Under N2 atmosphere, an oven-dried 20
mL vial was charged with epiandrosterone (100 mg, 0.344 mmol, 1.00
equiv), KF (40.0 mg, 0.689 mmol, 2.00 equiv), and PhenoFluor (220 mg,
0.516 mmol, 1.50 equiv). Toluene (7.0 mL) was added, followed by
N,N-diisopropylethylamine (89.0 mg, 120 μL, 0.689 mmol, 2.00 equiv). The
reaction mixture was stirred in a sealed vial and heated at 80 °C for 15
h. Once cooled to 23 °C, the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo.
The residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel, eluting with
hexanes/EtOAc 10:1 (v/v), to afford 84.6 mg of the title compound.
3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-androsterone (13), colorless solid (84% yield) Rf = 0.32
(hexanes/EtOAc 10:1 (v/v)). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 23
°C, δ): 4.83 (d, J = 46.9 Hz, 1H), 2.45 (dd, J = 19.0, 8.8 Hz, 1H), 2.08
(dt, J = 18.9, 9.3 Hz, 1H), 2.00-1.14 (m, 19H), 1.04 (dq, J = 12.2, 4.4
Hz, 1H), 0.87 (s, 3H), 0.82 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ):
221.4, 89.4 (d, JCF = 162.9 Hz), 54.3, 51.6, 47.9, 39.5, 36.0, 36.0,
35.2, 34.0 (d, JCF = 21.1 Hz), 32.5, 31.7, 30.9, 28.2, 27.2 (d, JCF =
22.0 Hz), 21.9, 20.2, 13.9, 11.3. 19F NMR (375 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ):
177.4. Mass Spectrometry: HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z): Calcd for [C19H29FO +
H]+, 293.2275. Found, 293.2269.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Late-Stage Deoxyfluorination of Alcohols with PhenoFluor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
