$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-(4-bromophenyl)-6-(1-fluoroethyl)-2-methylpyrimidine
(±)-4a from (±)-5. To a solution of (±)-5 (0.34 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (7 mL) at
-10°C under argon was added, dropwise, DAST (0.76 mmol, 2.2 eq). After 1h
at -10°C the mixture was neutralized with NaHCO3. The organic layer was
separated, washed, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under vacuum to
afford an orange oil. After purification on a silica gel column
(Pentane/AcOEt 9/1) pyrimidine (±)-4a was obtained as a pale yellow solid
(86.0 mg, 86% yield)
4-(4-bromophenyl)-6-(1-fluoroethyl)-2-methylpyrimidine (±)-4a, yield 86.0
mg, 86% Rf = 0.29 (9/1 pentane/AcOEt). Mp: 45 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300
MHz): δ 8.03-7.97 (m, 2H); 7.66 (bs, 1H); 7.65-7.60 (m, 2H); 5.63 (dq,
JHF = 48.1 Hz, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H); 2.78 (s, 3H); 1.71 (dd, JHF = 24.5 Hz, J
= 6.6 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 170.1 (d, JCF = 24.7 Hz); 168.0
(d, JCF = 3.0 Hz); 163.9 (d, JCF = 1.5 Hz); 135.9, 132.2, 128.8, 125.6,
108.2 (d, JCF = 8.3 Hz); 90.5 (d, JCF = 172.1 Hz); 26.1, 21.4 (d, JCF =
26.4 Hz). 19F NMR (CDCl3, 282 MHz): δ -183.61 (dq, J1 = 48.0 Hz, J2 =
24.0 Hz). HRMS (EI). Calcd for C13H12N2F79Br [M+]: m/z 294.0168. Found:
m/z 294.0172.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Flexible Synthesis of Pyrimidines with Chiral Monofluorinated and
Difluoromethyl Side Chains
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bannwarth, Pierre; Valleix, Alain; Gree, Danielle; Gree, Rene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(12), 4646-4649

