$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Deoxofluoro-arylsufinylation of ethylene glycol A solution of 0.991 g
(3.96 mmol) of 1k in 1 mL of dry dichloromethane was slowly added to a
stirred solution of 0.246 g (3.96 mmol) of ethylene glycol and 0.800 g
(7.72 mmol) of triethylamine in 3 mL of dry dichloromethane in a
fluoropolymer vessel cooled on an ice bath. The reaction mixture was
stirred on an ice bath for 1 h and then at room temperature for 15 h. An
aq. saturated sodium bicarbonate solution was added to the reaction
mixture, which was then extracted with dichloromethane. The organic layer
was separated, washed with water, dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate,
and filtered. Removal of solvent at reduced pressure gave a residue,
which was then thin-layered chromatographed on silica gel using
ether:hexane (1:5) as an eluent to give 2-fluoroethyl
4-tert-butyl-2,6-dimethylbenzenesulfinate (18) as a colorless solid.
Yield: 0.927 g (86%). 2-fluoroethyl
4-tert-butyl-2,6-dimethylbenzenesulfinate (18), yield 0.927 g (86%). M.p.
65-66 °C; 19F NMR (CDCl3) δ -224.20 (tt, J = 59.6, 35.8 Hz, 1F); 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 7.04 (s, 2H), 4.64 (dt, J = 47.1, 3.8 Hz, 2H), 4.15-4.45 (m,
2H), 2.63 (s, 6H), 1.29 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 155.3, 137.9, 137.6,
127.3, 82.3 (d, J = 171.9 Hz), 67.1 (d, J = 20.2 Hz), 34.8, 31.1, 19.5;
IR (nujol) 2956, 1593, 1481, 1414, 1364, 1283, 1229, 1127, 1065, 876, 736
cm-1. Anal Calcd for C14H21FO2S: C, 61.73%; H, 7.77%. Found: C, 61.97%;
H, 7.73%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (toxic byproduct HF), alternative reaction conditions without Et3N
gave lower yield, fluoropolymer vessel used, alternative preparation
shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Umemoto, Teruo; Singh, Rajendra P.; Xu, Yong; Saito, Norimichi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2010), 132(51), 18199-18205

