$DATUM (-)-(6aR,8S,9S,9aR)-8-Bromo-9-fluoro-2,2,4,4-tetraisopropyl-7-methylenehexahydrocyclopenta[f][1,3,5,2,4]trioxadisilocine
(16). To a stirred solution of compound 13 (0.5 g, 1.23 mmol) in dry DCM
was added carbon tetrabromide (1.63 g, 4.9 mmol), followed by the
addition of triphenylphosphine (1.29 g, 4.9 mmol) at 0 °C. The mixture
was warmed to room temperature and stirred for 3 h. The reaction mixture
was neutralized with triethylamine and passed through a small bed of
silica gel. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure, and the
residue was purified by flash silica gel column chromatography (4%
EtOAc/96% hexane) to give compound. Yield: (0.49 g, 86%) as an oil. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.93-1.01 (m, 28H), 2.65-2.63 (m, 1H), 3.87 (dd, J
= 4.5, 14.0 Hz, 1H), 3.96 (dd, J = 4.0, 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.11-4.07 (m, 1H),
4.60 (ddd, J = 2.0, 6.5, and 17.0 Hz, 1H), 4.95 (dt, J = 6.5, 54.5 Hz,
1H), 5.22 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.40 (s, 1H); 19F NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
-187.0 (dt, J = 17.5, 56.0 Hz, 1F); 13C{1H} NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 11.50,
11.53, 11.7, 11.8, 12.2, 12.4, 15.8, 15.9, 16.02, 16.05, 16.2, 16.3,
16.4, 28.6, 47.8, 59.3, 101.7 (d, J = 194.6 Hz), 113.6, 142.4; HRMS (EI)
calcd for (C19H36BrFO3Si2 + H)+ 467.1449, found 467.1434.
