$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAS_Reaction_Number
$DATUM 31-031-CAS-3324248
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):STEPS
$DATUM 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):STAGES
$DATUM 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):PRO(1):YIELD
$DATUM 85
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a reactor with a TeflonTM PFA tube with a diameter of 10 mm sealed at
one end, 1a (137 mg, 1 mmol) and DFBA (478 mg, 2.4 mmol) were introduced.
The open end of the reactor was connected to a reflux condenser. Then,
the reactor part was submitted to microwave-irradiation (IDX microwave
oven for organic synthesis IMCR-25003) for 10 min and during the
irradiation the temperature was kept at 70 °C. After cooling, the
reaction mixture was poured into an aq solution of NaHCO3. The product
was extracted with Et2O (3 ×) and the combined ethereal layers were dried
over MgSO4. Purification by column chromatography (silica gel,
hexane-Et2O) gave 2a. N-(2-Fluoroethyl)-N-phenylbenzamide (2a), yield 207
mg, 0.85 mmol, 85%. IR (neat): 1649, 1494, 1377 cm-1. 1H NMR: δ =
7.32-7.09 (m, 10 H), 4.76 (dt, J = 47.6, 4.9 Hz, 2 H), 4.20 (dt, J =
25.6, 4.9 Hz, 2 H). 19C NMR: δ = 170.94, 144.08, 135.80, 129.94, 129.31
(2 C), 128.90 (2 C), 127.89 (2 C), 127.83 (2 C), 126.91, 81.52 (d, J =
168.7 Hz), 51.57 (d, J = 20.7 Hz). 19F NMR: δ = - 222.60 to -222.98 (m, 1
F). HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C15H14NOF: 243.1059; found: 243.1057.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, IDX microwave oven used, no
solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (fluoroalkyl)amines by deoxyfluorination of amino alcohols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nomoto, Takashi; Fukuhara, Tsuyoshi; Hara, Shoji
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2006), (11), 1744-1746

